to Snoqualmie Valley Community Plan P-Suffix Conditions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Appendix J:  Amendments
to Newcastle Community Plan P-Suffix Conditions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Appendix K:  Amendments
to Tahoma/Raven Heights Community Plan P-Suffix Conditions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Appendix L:  Amendments
to Enumclaw Community Plan P-Suffix Conditions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Appendix M:  Amendments
to West Hill Community Plan P-Suffix Conditions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Appendix N:  Amendments
to Resource Lands Community Plan P-Suffix Conditions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Appendix O:  1994
Parcel List, as amended December 19, 1994.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Appendix P:  Amendments
considered by the council January 9, 1995.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Area
zoning adopted by Ordinance 11653, including potential zoning, is contained in
Appendices A and O.  Amendments to area-wide P-suffix conditions adopted as
part of community plan area zoning are contained in Appendices B through N. 
Existing P-suffix conditions whether adopted through reclassifications or
community plan area zoning are retained by Ordinance 11653 except as amended in
Appendices B through N.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  The
department is hereby directed to correct the official zoning map in accordance
with Appendices A through P of Ordinance 11653.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  The 1995
area zoning amendments attached to Ordinance 12061 in Appendix A are adopted as
the official zoning control for those portions of unincorporated King County
defined therein.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  Amendments
to the 1994 King County Comprehensive Plan area zoning, Ordinance 11653
Appendices A through P, as contained in Attachment A to Ordinance 12170 are
hereby adopted to comply with the Decision and Order of the Central Puget Sound
Growth Management Hearings Board in Vashon-Maury Island, et. al. v. King
County, Case No. 95-3-0008.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  The Vashon
Area Zoning adopted in Ordinance 12824, as amended, including as amended by
Ordinance 17842, Ordinance 18427 and Ordinance 19119, is adopted as the
official zoning control for that portion of unincorporated King County defined
therein.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G.  The 1996
area zoning amendments attached to Ordinance 12531 in Appendix A are adopted as
the official zoning control for those portions of unincorporated King County
defined therein.  Existing p-suffix conditions whether adopted through
reclassifications or area zoning are retained by Ordinance 12531.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H.  The <span
style='text-transform:uppercase'>b</span>lack Diamond Urban Growth Area Zoning
Map attached to Ordinance 12533 as Appendix B is adopted as the official zoning
control for those portions of unincorporated King County defined therein. 
Existing p-suffix conditions whether adopted through reclassifications or area
zoning are retained by Ordinance 12533.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            I.  The King
County Zoning Atlas is amended to include the area shown in Appendix B as UR -
Urban Reserve, one DU per 5 acres.  Existing p-suffix conditions whether
adopted through reclassifications or area zoning are retained by Ordinance
12535.  The language from Ordinance 12535, Section 1.D., shall be placed on the
King County Zoning Atlas page #32 with a reference marker on the area affected
by Ordinance 12535.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            J.  The
Northshore Community Plan Area Zoning is amended to add the Suffix &quot;-DPA,
Demonstration Project Area,&quot; to the properties identified on Map A
attached to Ordinance 12627.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            K.  The
special district overlays, as designated on the map attached to Ordinance 12809
in Appendix A, are hereby adopted pursuant to K.C.C. 21A.38.020 and 21A.38.040.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            L.  The White
Center Community Plan Area Zoning, as revised in the Attachments to Ordinance
11568, is the official zoning for those portions of White Center in
unincorporated King County defined herein.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            M.  Ordinance
12824 completes the zoning conversion process begun in Ordinance 11653, as set
forth in K.C.C. 21A.01.070, by retaining, repealing, replacing or amending
previously adopted p-suffix conditions or property-specific development
standards pursuant to K.C.C. 21A.38.020 and K.C.C. 21A.38.030 as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Resolutions
31072, 32219, 33877, 33999, 34493, 34639, 35137 and 37156 adopting individual
zone reclassifications are hereby repealed and p-suffix conditions are replaced
by the property specific development standards as set forth in Appendix A to
Ordinance 12824;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  All
ordinances adopting individual zone reclassifications effective before February
2, 1995, including but not limited to Ordinances 43, 118, 148, 255, 633, 1483,
1543, 1582, 1584, 1728, 1788, 2487, 2508, 2548, 2608, 2677, 2701, 2703, 2765,
2781, 2840, 2884, 2940, 2958, 2965, 2997, 3239, 3262, 3313, 3360, 3424, 3494,
3496, 3501, 3557, 3561, 3641, 3643, 3744, 3779, 3901, 3905, 3953, 3988, 4008,
4043, 4051, 4053, 4082, 4094, 4137, 4289, 4290, 4418, 4560, 4589, 4703, 4706,
4764, 4767, 4867, 4812, 4885, 4888, 4890, 4915, 4933, 4956, 4970, 4978, 5087,
5114, 5144, 5148, 5171, 5184, 5242, 5346, 5353, 5378, 5453, 5663, 5664, 5689,
5744, 5752, 5755, 5765, 5854, 5984, 5985, 5986, 6059, 6074, 6113, 6151, 6275,
6468, 6497, 6618, 6671, 6698, 6832, 6885, 6916, 6966, 6993, 7008, 7087, 7115,
7207, 7328, 7375, 7382, 7396, 7583, 7653, 7677, 7694, 7705, 7757, 7758, 7821,
7831, 7868, 7944, 7972, 8158, 8307, 8361, 8375, 8427, 8452, 8465, 8571, 8573,
8603, 8718, 8733, 8786, 8796, 8825, 8858, 8863, 8865, 8866, 9030, 9095, 9189,
9276, 9295, 9476, 9622, 9656, 9823, 9991, 10033, 10194, 10287, 10419, 10598, 10668,
10781, 10813, 10970, 11024, 11025, 11271 and 11651, are hereby repealed and
p-suffix conditions are replaced by the property specific development standards
as set forth in Appendix A to Ordinance 12824;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  All
ordinances establishing individual reclassifications effective after February
2, 1995, are hereby amended, as set forth in Appendix C to Ordinance 12824, to
retain, repeal or amend the property specific development standards (p-suffix
conditions) contained therein;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  All
ordinances adopting area zoning pursuant to Resolution 25789 or converted by
Ordinance 11653 are repealed as set forth in subsection M.4.a. through n. of
this section.  All p-suffix conditions contained therein are repealed or
replaced by adopting the property specific development standards as set forth
in Appendix A to Ordinance 12824, the special district overlays as designated
in Appendix B to Ordinance 12824 or the special requirements as designated in
Appendix A to Ordinance 12822.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  The
Highline Area Zoning attached to Ordinance 3530, as amended, is hereby
repealed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  The
Shoreline Community Plan Area Zoning, attached to Ordinance 5080 as Appendix B,
as amended, is hereby repealed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                c.  The
Newcastle Community Plan Area Zoning, attached to Ordinance 6422 as Appendix B,
as amended is hereby repealed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                d.  The
Tahoma/Raven Heights Community Plan Area Zoning, attached to Ordinance 6986 as
Appendix B, as amended, is hereby repealed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                e.  The
Revised Federal Way area zoning, adopted by Ordinance 7746, as amended, is
hereby repealed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                f.  The
Revised Vashon Community Plan Area Zoning, attached to Ordinance 7837 as
Appendix B, as amended, is hereby repealed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                g.  The
Bear Creek Community Plan Area Zoning, attached to Ordinance 8846 as Appendix B,
as amended, is hereby repealed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                h.  The
Resource Lands Area Zoning, adopted by Ordinance 8848, as amended, is hereby
repealed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                i.  The
Snoqualmie Valley Community Plan Area Zoning, as adopted by Ordinance 9118, is
hereby repealed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                j.  The
Enumclaw Community Plan Area Zoning attached to Ordinance 9499, as amended, is
hereby repealed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                k.  The
Soos Creek Community Plan Update Area Zoning, adopted by Ordinance 10197,
Appendix B, as amended, is hereby repealed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                l.  The
Northshore Area Zoning adopted by Ordinance 10703 as Appendices B and E, as
amended, is hereby repealed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                m.  The
East Sammamish Community Plan Update Area Zoning, as revised in Appendix B
attached to Ordinance 10847, as amended, is hereby repealed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                n.  The
West Hill Community Plan Area Zoning adopted in Ordinance 11166, as amended, is
hereby repealed; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              5.  All
ordinances adopting area zoning pursuant to Title 21A and not converted by
Ordinance 11653, including community or Comprehensive Plan area zoning and all
subsequent amendments thereto, are amended as set forth in subsection M.5.a.
through f. of this section.  All property specific development standards
(p-suffix conditions) are retained, repealed, amended or replaced by the
property specific development standards as set forth in Appendix A to Ordinance
12824, the special district overlays as designated in Appendix B to Ordinance
12824 or the special requirements as designated in Appendix A to Ordinance
12822.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  The
White Center Community Plan Area Zoning, contained in the Attachments to
Ordinance 11568, as amended as set forth in Appendix D to Ordinance 12824,
Ordinance 19119 and Ordinance 19555.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  All
property specific development standards established in Ordinance 11653, as
amended, are hereby amended as set forth in Appendix E to Ordinance 12824.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                c.  All
property specific development standards established in Attachment A to
Ordinance 11747, as amended, are hereby amended as set forth in Appendix F.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                d.  All
property specific development standards established in Ordinance 12061, as
amended, are hereby amended as set forth in Appendix G to Ordinance 12824.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                e.  All
property specific development standards established in Ordinance 12065, as
amended, are hereby amended as set forth in K.C.C. 20.12.170.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                f.  All
property specific development standards established in Attachment A to
Ordinance 12170, as amended, are hereby amended as set forth in Appendix H.  (Ord.
19555 § 4, 2022:  Ord. 19146 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 6, 2020:  Ord. 18623 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>
5, 2017:  Ord. 18427 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 6, 2016:  Ord. 17842 § 3, 2014:  Ord. 12824 § 2, 1997: 
Ord. 12809 § 2, 1997:  Ord. 12627 § 6, 1996:  Ord. 12535 § 4, 1996:  Ord. 12533
§ 2, 1996:  Ord. 12531 § 2, 1996:  Ord. 12395 § 3, 1996:  Ord. 12170 § 2, 1995:
Ord. 12061 § 2, 1995:  Ord. 11653 § 6, 1995).</span></p>

<p class=footnote style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=footnote style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Reviser’s notes:</span></b></p>

<p class=footnote style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*All ordinances and attachments, including appendices,
cited in this section are available in the King County Archives.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>20.12.050 
Zoning, potential zoning, property-specific development standards, special
district overlays, regional use designations and interim zoning.</b>  Zoning
adopted pursuant to this section shall constitute official zoning for all of
unincorporated King County.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Official
zoning, including but not limited to p-suffix, so-suffix and potential zoning,
is contained in geographic information system data layers maintained by King
County and is depicted on the official zoning maps, as maintained by the
department of </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>local services, permitting division</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>. 
In case of a discrepancy between a data layer and the original map or document
adopted by ordinance, the original map or document shall control.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Appendix A
of Ordinance 12824*, as amended by Ordinance 15028, is hereby adopted to
constitute and contain all property-specific development standards (p-suffix
conditions) applicable in unincorporated King County.  The property specific
development standards (p-suffix conditions) in effect or hereinafter amended
shall be maintained by the department of </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>local services, permitting
division,</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> in the Property Specific Development Conditions
notebook.  Any adoption, amendment or repeal of property-specific development
standards shall amend, pursuant to this section, Appendix A of Ordinance 12824*
as currently in effect or hereafter amended.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Appendix B
of Ordinance 12824*, as amended by Ordinance 14044* and as amended by Ordinance
15028*, is hereby adopted to constitute and contain special district overlays
applied through Ordinance 12824*.  The special district overlays in effect or
hereinafter amended shall be maintained by the department of </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>local
services, permitting division,</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> in the Special District Overlay
Application Maps notebook.  Any adoption, amendment or repeal of special
district overlays shall amend, pursuant to this section, Appendix B of
Ordinance 12824* as currently in effect or hereafter amended.  (Ord. 18791 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 145,
2018:  Ord. 17485 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 6, 2012:  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Ord. 17420 § 81, 2012: </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> Ord.
15028 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 4, 2004:  Ord. 14044 § 3, 2001:  Ord. 12824 § 3, 1997).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Available in the King
County Archives.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            20.12.200  Shoreline
master program.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-indent:.5in'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>A. 
The King County shoreline master program consists of the following elements, enacted
on or before</span> <span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>December 15, 2025:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  The King
County Comprehensive Plan chapter six;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  K.C.C.
chapter 21A.25;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  The
following sections of K.C.C. chapter 21A.24:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  K.C.C.
21A.24.045;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  K.C.C.
21A.24.051;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                c.  K.C.C.
21A.24.070.A., B.2., C.2., D. and E.;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                d.  K.C.C.
21A.24.125;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                e.  K.C.C.
21A.24.130;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                f.  K.C.C.
21A.24.133;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                g.  K.C.C.
21A.24.183;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                h.  K.C.C.
21A.24.200;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                i.  K.C.C.
21A.24.275;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                j.  K.C.C.
21A.24.280;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                k.  K.C.C.
21A.24.285;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                l.  K.C.C.
21A.24.290;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                m.  K.C.C.
21A.24.292;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                n.  K.C.C.
21A.24.295;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                o.  K.C.C.
21A.24.300;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                p.  K.C.C.
21A.24.305;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                q.  K.C.C.
21A.24.307;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                r.  K.C.C.
21A.24.316;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                s.  K.C.C.
